From: ScorchDroid <noreply@example.com>
Subject: [PATCH] android: the between-rounds scoreboard

ShowScoreAction is queued by ServerStateScore at the end of every round,
and again at the end of the match, and holds the game there for
RoundScoreTime (5s by default) or ScoreTime (15s). Upstream's client half
of that action stimulates ClientState::StimScore, which is what actually
puts the score table on screen - and, like every other piece of
presentation in src/common/actions, it sits behind #ifndef S3D_SERVER and
is absent from this build.

So the port simulated the pause exactly right and showed nothing during
it: the score table existed, but only if the player thought to open it by
hand, by which point the round was over. This raises a flag instead, which
the UI polls on the tick it already runs (see ScoreboardState.h), opening
the score dialog over an idle HUD and taking it down when play resumes. A
dialog the player opened themselves is never replaced.

Deliberately without upstream's !getServerMode() guard: that guard exists
to stop a hosting client doing the work twice, and on this port - which
runs these actions on the server context - it would simply switch the
whole thing off. Patch 0016 documents that trap at length.

No game logic changes: the action's timing, its scoreFinished() call and
the state machine around it are untouched.

diff --git a/src/common/actions/ShowScoreAction.cpp b/src/common/actions/ShowScoreAction.cpp
index 2e394cf3..576753e0 100644
--- a/src/common/actions/ShowScoreAction.cpp
+++ b/src/common/actions/ShowScoreAction.cpp
@@ -19,6 +19,11 @@
 ////////////////////////////////////////////////////////////////////////////////
 
 #include <actions/ShowScoreAction.hpp>
+#ifdef S3D_SERVER
+	// Android build: upstream raises its score screen from the client half
+	// of this action, which is compiled out here - see ScoreboardState.h.
+	#include <ScoreboardState.h>
+#endif
 #include <engine/ScorchedContext.hpp>
 #include <server/ScorchedServer.hpp>
 #include <server/ServerState.hpp>
@@ -82,6 +87,13 @@ void ShowScoreAction::init()
 		ScorchedClient::instance()->getGameState().stimulate(ClientState::StimWait);
 		ScorchedClient::instance()->getGameState().stimulate(ClientState::StimScore);
 	}
+#else
+	// Android build: the same thing the two stimulations above do - put the
+	// score table on screen and leave it there for as long as this action
+	// runs. Deliberately without upstream's !getServerMode() guard, which
+	// exists to stop a hosting client doing this twice and on this port
+	// would simply switch it off (see patch 0016).
+	ScorchDroidScoreboard::show(finalScore_);
 #endif
 }
 
@@ -92,6 +104,11 @@ void ShowScoreAction::simulate(fixed frameTime, bool &remove)
 	if (scoreTime_ <= 0)
 	{
 		remove = true;
+#ifdef S3D_SERVER
+		// Play resumes, so the board comes down. Upstream's client leaves
+		// its score state the same way, on the next round's stimulation.
+		ScorchDroidScoreboard::hide();
+#endif
 		if (context_->getServerMode())
 		{
 			ScorchedServer::instance()->getServerState().scoreFinished();
